{"id":"0fcefcbcd177ba8fc7e5c41ba4ef050173e86b32","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"0fcefcbcd177ba8fc7e5c41ba4ef050173e86b32","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".buildkite/test_areas/expert_parallelism.yaml","lines":["@@ -13,10 +13,14 @@ steps:","   - tests/distributed/test_eplb_algo.py","   - tests/distributed/test_eplb_migration_scheduler.py","   - tests/distributed/test_eplb_utils.py","+  - tests/distributed/test_eplb_extension_hooks.py","+  - vllm/config/parallel.py","+  - vllm/platforms/interface.py","   commands:","   - pytest -v -s distributed/test_eplb_algo.py","   - pytest -v -s distributed/test_eplb_migration_scheduler.py","   - pytest -v -s distributed/test_eplb_utils.py","+  - pytest -v -s distributed/test_eplb_extension_hooks.py","   mirror:","     amd:","       automatic_shard: true","@@ -30,6 +34,9 @@ steps:","       - vllm/distributed/eplb","       - tests/distributed/test_eplb_algo.py","       - tests/distributed/test_eplb_utils.py","+      - tests/distributed/test_eplb_extension_hooks.py","+      - vllm/config/parallel.py","+      - vllm/platforms/interface.py","       - vllm/platforms/rocm.py"," "," - label: \":nvidia: (L4) [Nightly] EPLB Execution\""],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/design/plugin_system.md","lines":["@@ -106,6 +106,12 @@ Every plugin has three parts:","     - `get_attn_backend_cls`: This function should return the attention backend class's fully qualified name.","     - `get_device_communicator_cls`: This function should return the device communicator class's fully qualified name."," ","+    For out-of-tree EPLB, implement `supports_eplb()` and `check_and_update_eplb_config(parallel_config)` to select and validate policy and communicator names. An unset policy is `None` until this hook selects the platform default; preserve explicitly configured names. When EPLB is enabled, this hook selects the default communicator and validates names and configuration combinations; `EPLBConfig` enforces field types and numeric bounds. Built-in names retain their existing defaults and async communicator restrictions; a platform override owns validation of its custom names and combinations.","+","+    To use an `EplbState` subclass, construct it in the plugin's worker or controller. The platform configuration hooks do not select the state class; the upstream `EPLBController` constructs the base `EplbState`.","+","+    An `EplbState` subclass can implement `create_policy()` and `create_model_communicator()`. `create_policy()` returns one `AbstractEplbPolicy` instance shared by the models in that state. Device-specific expert mapping and load recording belong to a registered router subclass overriding `_apply_eplb_mapping()`; the router retains ownership of its layer state. Synchronous, profiling and asynchronous planning call `policy.rebalance_experts(stats, old_global_expert_indices)` directly. Asynchronous planning runs on the background worker thread; synchronous planning and profiling run on the main thread. `EplbStats` holds one load/topology snapshot; downstream policies can accept dataclass subclasses carrying additional planning inputs. Before calling the policy, the worker replaces the snapshot's load field with its CPU copy on the worker stream. This preserves the stats instance, its subclass and any additional fields. The default policy consumes aggregate CPU loads of shape `[layers, experts]` and returns a CPU integer placement tensor. Keep policy configuration on the policy instance and per-model, per-round inputs in the snapshot. Set `EplbState.model_state_cls` to an `EplbModelState` subclass to customize model-local commits. `_commit_eplb_maps()` installs a full-model placement and `_commit_eplb_maps_for_layer()` installs one layer. `_move_to_workspace()` consumes that model's pending transfer result; commit overrides must submit device-specific updates before returning so buffer acknowledgement remains after weight installation and map updates.","+"," 4. Implement the worker class `MyDummyWorker` in `my_dummy_worker.py`. The worker class should inherit from [WorkerBase][vllm.v1.worker.worker_base.WorkerBase]. Please follow the interface to implement the functions one by one. Basically, all interfaces in the base class should be implemented, since they are called here and there in vLLM. To make sure a model can be executed, the basic functions should be implemented are:"," ","     - `init_device`: This function is called to set up the device for the worker."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_eplb_algo.py","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@","     _compute_eplb_load_stats,  # pyright: ignore[reportPrivateUsage]","     compute_logical_maps,"," )","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy import EplbStats"," from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy.default import DefaultEplbPolicy"," from vllm.platforms import current_platform"," ","@@ -45,8 +46,8 @@ def test_basic_rebalance():","     num_nodes = 2","     num_gpus = 8"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     log2phy, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -100,8 +101,8 @@ def test_single_gpu_case():","     num_nodes = 1","     num_gpus = 1"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     log2phy, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -123,8 +124,8 @@ def test_equal_weights():","     num_nodes = 2","     num_gpus = 4"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -147,8 +148,8 @@ def test_extreme_weight_imbalance():","     num_nodes = 2","     num_gpus = 4"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -176,8 +177,8 @@ def test_multiple_layers():","     num_nodes = 2","     num_gpus = 4"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -202,7 +203,7 @@ def test_parameter_validation():","     # Test non-divisible case - this should handle normally without throwing","     # errors because the function will fall back to global load balancing","     # strategy","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(weight, 8, 3, 2, 4)","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(EplbStats(weight, 8, 3, 2, 4))","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])","     assert phy2log.shape == (1, 8)","     assert logcnt.shape == (1, 4)","@@ -210,7 +211,9 @@ def test_parameter_validation():","     # Test cases that will actually cause errors:","     # num_physical_experts not divisible by num_gpus","     with pytest.raises(AssertionError):","-        DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(weight, 7, 2, 2, 4)  # 7 not divisible by 4","+        DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+            EplbStats(weight, 7, 2, 2, 4)","+        )  # 7 not divisible by 4"," "," "," def test_small_scale_hierarchical():","@@ -225,8 +228,8 @@ def test_small_scale_hierarchical():","     num_nodes = 2  # 2 nodes","     num_gpus = 4  # 4 GPUs"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -253,8 +256,8 @@ def test_global_load_balance_fallback():","     num_nodes = 2","     num_gpus = 4"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -278,8 +281,8 @@ def test_device_compatibility(device):","     num_nodes = 1","     num_gpus = 2"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     _, logcnt = compute_logical_maps(phy2log, weight.shape[-1])"," ","@@ -295,7 +298,7 @@ def test_additional_cases():","     weight1 = torch.tensor(","         [[50, 100, 75, 120, 90, 60, 80, 110, 40, 70, 95, 85, 65, 55, 45, 35]]","     )","-    phy2log1 = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(weight1, 24, 8, 4, 8)","+    phy2log1 = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(EplbStats(weight1, 24, 8, 4, 8))","     _, logcnt1 = compute_logical_maps(phy2log1, weight1.shape[-1])"," ","     assert phy2log1.shape == (1, 24)","@@ -309,7 +312,7 @@ def test_additional_cases():","             [12, 25, 50, 100, 150, 200],  # Increasing weights","         ]","     )","-    phy2log2 = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(weight2, 10, 3, 1, 2)","+    phy2log2 = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(EplbStats(weight2, 10, 3, 1, 2))","     _, logcnt2 = compute_logical_maps(phy2log2, weight2.shape[-1])"," ","     assert phy2log2.shape == (2, 10)","@@ -369,8 +372,8 @@ def test_compute_logical_maps_with_negative_indices():","     num_nodes = 2","     num_gpus = 8"," ","-    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy.rebalance_experts(","-        weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus","+    phy2log = DefaultEplbPolicy().rebalance_experts(","+        EplbStats(weight, num_replicas, num_groups, num_nodes, num_gpus)","     )","     print(phy2log)"," "],"additions":25,"deletions":22,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_eplb_extension_hooks.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,330 @@","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+","+from dataclasses import dataclass","+","+import pytest","+import torch","+from transformers import LlamaConfig","+","+import vllm.config.parallel as parallel_config_module","+from vllm.config import ParallelConfig, VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config","+from vllm.config.parallel import EPLBConfig","+from vllm.distributed import (","+    cleanup_dist_env_and_memory,","+    init_distributed_environment,","+    initialize_model_parallel,","+)","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.async_worker import run_rebalance_experts","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.eplb_communicator import TorchDistGlooStagedEplbCommunicator","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.eplb_state import (","+    EplbModelState,","+    EplbState,","+    EplbStats,","+    compute_logical_maps,","+)","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.eplb_utils import CpuGpuEvent","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.policy import DefaultEplbPolicy","+from vllm.distributed.eplb.rebalance_execute import AsyncEplbLayerResult, transfer_layer","+from vllm.distributed.parallel_state import get_ep_group","+from vllm.platforms import current_platform","+from vllm.platforms.interface import Platform, PlatformEnum","+","+","+class _Platform(Platform):","+    _enum = PlatformEnum.OOT","+","+    @classmethod","+    def supports_eplb(cls):","+        return True","+","+    @classmethod","+    def check_and_update_eplb_config(cls, parallel_config):","+        config = parallel_config.eplb_config","+        if config.policy is None:","+            config.policy = \"custom\"","+        if config.policy != \"custom\" or config.communicator not in (","+            None,","+            \"custom_comm\",","+        ):","+            raise ValueError(\"unsupported custom EPLB configuration\")","+        config.communicator = \"custom_comm\"","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    \"policy, communicator\", [(None, None), (\"custom\", None), (\"custom\", \"custom_comm\")]","+)","+def test_platform_can_validate_out_of_tree_names(monkeypatch, policy, communicator):","+    monkeypatch.setattr(parallel_config_module, \"current_platform\", _Platform())","+    config = ParallelConfig(","+        enable_eplb=True,","+        enable_expert_parallel=True,","+        tensor_parallel_size=2,","+        distributed_executor_backend=\"uni\",","+        eplb_config=EPLBConfig(policy=policy, communicator=communicator),","+    )","+    assert config.eplb_config.policy == \"custom\"","+    assert config.eplb_config.communicator == \"custom_comm\"","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"field_name\", [\"policy\", \"communicator\"])","+def test_builtin_platform_rejects_unknown_names(field_name):","+    config = ParallelConfig(eplb_config=EPLBConfig(**{field_name: \"unknown\"}))","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=f\"Unknown EPLB {field_name}\"):","+        Platform.check_and_update_eplb_config(config)","+","+","+def test_platform_can_reject_eplb_even_on_cuda(monkeypatch):","+    class UnsupportedCuda(Platform):","+        _enum = PlatformEnum.CUDA","+","+        @classmethod","+        def supports_eplb(cls):","+            return False","+","+    monkeypatch.setattr(parallel_config_module, \"current_platform\", UnsupportedCuda())","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"not supported on this platform\"):","+        ParallelConfig(","+            enable_eplb=True,","+            tensor_parallel_size=2,","+            distributed_executor_backend=\"uni\",","+        )","+","+","+def test_xpu_preserves_eplb_and_xccl_auto_selection():","+    class XpuPlatform(Platform):","+        _enum = PlatformEnum.XPU","+","+    config = ParallelConfig()","+    assert XpuPlatform.supports_eplb()","+    XpuPlatform.check_and_update_eplb_config(config)","+    assert config.eplb_config.communicator == \"torch_xccl\"","+    assert config.eplb_config.policy == \"default\"","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    \"communicator, use_async\",","+    [","+        (\"torch_gloo\", True),","+        (\"torch_xccl\", True),","+        (\"nixl\", True),","+        (\"torch_nccl\", False),","+        (\"pynccl\", False),","+    ],","+)","+def test_explicit_builtin_communicator_is_preserved(communicator, use_async):","+    config = ParallelConfig(","+        eplb_config=EPLBConfig(communicator=communicator, use_async=use_async)","+    )","+    Platform.check_and_update_eplb_config(config)","+    assert config.eplb_config.communicator == communicator","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"communicator\", [\"torch_nccl\", \"pynccl\"])","+def test_async_nccl_restrictions_remain(communicator):","+    config = ParallelConfig(eplb_config=EPLBConfig(communicator=communicator))","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"incompatible with async EPLB\"):","+        Platform.check_and_update_eplb_config(config)","+","+","+def test_llm_rejects_async_nccl_communicator(vllm_runner, monkeypatch, tmp_path):","+    \"\"\"Reject an invalid async communicator before loading model weights.\"\"\"","+","+    class BuiltinPlatform(Platform):","+        _enum = PlatformEnum.CUDA","+","+    monkeypatch.setattr(parallel_config_module, \"current_platform\", BuiltinPlatform())","+    LlamaConfig(","+        architectures=[\"LlamaForCausalLM\"],","+        hidden_size=32,","+        intermediate_size=64,","+        num_hidden_layers=1,","+        num_attention_heads=2,","+        num_key_value_heads=2,","+        max_position_embeddings=32,","+    ).save_pretrained(tmp_path)","+    eplb_config = EPLBConfig(communicator=\"torch_nccl\")","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"incompatible with async EPLB\"):","+        vllm_runner(","+            str(tmp_path),","+            max_model_len=32,","+            skip_tokenizer_init=True,","+            tensor_parallel_size=2,","+            enable_expert_parallel=True,","+            enable_eplb=True,","+            distributed_executor_backend=\"uni\",","+            eplb_config=eplb_config,","+        )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"interval\", [0, -1])","+def test_balancedness_interval_must_be_positive(interval):","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"log_balancedness_interval\"):","+        EPLBConfig(log_balancedness_interval=interval)","+","+","+@pytest.fixture","+def cpu_group(tmp_path):","+    with set_current_vllm_config(VllmConfig()):","+        init_distributed_environment(","+            world_size=1,","+            rank=0,","+            local_rank=0,","+            distributed_init_method=f\"file://{tmp_path}/store\",","+            backend=\"gloo\",","+        )","+        initialize_model_parallel(backend=\"gloo\")","+        try:","+            yield get_ep_group().cpu_group","+        finally:","+            cleanup_dist_env_and_memory()","+","+","+class _ExpertModel(torch.nn.Module):","+    \"\"\"Small real expert weight owner for control-plane and transfer checks.\"\"\"","+","+    def __init__(self):","+        super().__init__()","+        self.weight = torch.nn.Parameter(","+            torch.arange(16).reshape(4, 2, 2).float(), False","+        )","+        self.expert_weights = [[self.weight]]","+        self.num_moe_layers = 1","+","+","+class _ModelState(EplbModelState):","+    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):","+        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)","+        self.fail_commit = False","+        self.committed_layers = []","+        self.committed_maps = []","+","+    def _commit_eplb_maps_for_layer(self, target, layer):","+        super()._commit_eplb_maps_for_layer(target, layer)","+        assert not self.pending_result.consumed_event._recorded.is_set()","+        if self.fail_commit:","+            raise RuntimeError(\"device commit failed\")","+        self.committed_layers.append(layer)","+        self.committed_maps.append(self.physical_to_logical_map.clone())","+","+    def _commit_eplb_maps(self, target):","+        super()._commit_eplb_maps(target)","+        self.committed_layers.extend(range(self.model.num_moe_layers))","+        self.committed_maps.append(self.physical_to_logical_map.clone())","+","+","+class _State(EplbState):","+    model_state_cls = _ModelState","+","+    def __init__(self, policy=None):","+        self.selected_policy = policy or DefaultEplbPolicy()","+        super().__init__(ParallelConfig(), torch.device(\"cpu\"))","+","+    def create_policy(self):","+        return self.selected_policy","+","+","+@pytest.fixture","+def model_state(cpu_group):","+    model = _ExpertModel()","+    mapping = torch.arange(4).reshape(1, 4)","+    logical, replicas = compute_logical_maps(mapping, 4)","+    loads = torch.zeros(1, 4, dtype=torch.int64)","+    return _State.model_state_cls(","+        physical_to_logical_map=mapping,","+        physical_to_logical_map_buffer=mapping,","+        logical_to_physical_map=logical,","+        logical_replica_count=replicas,","+        expert_load_pass=loads,","+        expert_load_pass_buffer=loads,","+        expert_load_window=torch.zeros(4, 1, 4, dtype=torch.int64),","+        last_expert_load=torch.ones(1, 4, dtype=torch.int64),","+        model_name=\"expert-test\",","+        model=model,","+        expert_buffer=[torch.empty_like(model.weight)],","+        rebalanced=False,","+        eplb_stats=None,","+        device_index=None,","+        communicator=TorchDistGlooStagedEplbCommunicator(cpu_group),","+    )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"use_async\", [False, True])","+def test_policy_receives_extended_stats_without_losing_inputs(model_state, use_async):","+    @dataclass","+    class Stats(EplbStats):","+        metadata: tuple[int, ...] = ()","+","+    class Policy(DefaultEplbPolicy):","+        def rebalance_experts(self, stats, old_global_expert_indices=None):","+            assert stats is published_stats","+            assert isinstance(stats, Stats)","+            assert stats.metadata == (3, 7)","+            assert stats.global_expert_load_window.device.type == \"cpu\"","+            torch.testing.assert_close(stats.global_expert_load_window, loads)","+            return super().rebalance_experts(stats, old_global_expert_indices)","+","+    loads = torch.tensor([[13, 3, 4, 3]])","+    current = torch.tensor([[0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1]])","+    device = \"cpu\"","+    if use_async and (current_platform.is_cuda_alike() or current_platform.is_xpu()):","+        device = current_platform.device_type","+    published_stats = Stats(loads.to(device), 6, 1, 1, 2, metadata=(3, 7))","+    state = _State(Policy())","+    if use_async:","+        model_state.eplb_stats = published_stats","+        result = run_rebalance_experts(model_state, state, current, None)","+    else:","+        result = state.policy.rebalance_experts(published_stats, current)","+    default_state = EplbState(ParallelConfig(), torch.device(\"cpu\"))","+    assert isinstance(default_state.policy, DefaultEplbPolicy)","+    expected = default_state.policy.rebalance_experts(published_stats, current)","+    torch.testing.assert_close(result, expected, rtol=0, atol=0)","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"fail_commit\", [False, True])","+def test_async_commit_updates_maps_before_buffer_acknowledgement(","+    model_state, fail_commit","+):","+    model_state.fail_commit = fail_commit","+    target = torch.tensor([[1, 0, 3, 2]])","+    original = model_state.model.weight.detach().clone()","+    metadata = transfer_layer(","+        old_layer_indices=model_state.physical_to_logical_map[0],","+        new_layer_indices=target[0],","+        expert_weights=model_state.model.expert_weights[0],","+        expert_weights_buffer=model_state.expert_buffer,","+        communicator=model_state.communicator,","+        ep_group=get_ep_group().device_group,","+        stream=None,","+        is_profile=False,","+    )","+    result = AsyncEplbLayerResult(0, target[0], metadata, CpuGpuEvent())","+    model_state.pending_result = result","+    model_state.rebalanced = True","+    if fail_commit:","+        with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"commit failed\"):","+            model_state._move_to_workspace(0)","+    else:","+        model_state._move_to_workspace(0)","+    torch.testing.assert_close(model_state.model.weight, original[[1, 0, 3, 2]])","+    torch.testing.assert_close(model_state.physical_to_logical_map, target)","+    if fail_commit:","+        assert model_state.committed_layers == []","+        assert model_state.pending_result is result","+        assert not result.consumed_event._recorded.is_set()","+    else:","+        assert model_state.committed_layers == [0]","+        torch.testing.assert_close(model_state.committed_maps[0], target)","+        assert model_state.pending_result is None","+        assert result.consumed_event._recorded.is_set()","+","+","+def test_sync_commit_updates_maps_before_device_work(model_state):","+    target = torch.tensor([[1, 0, 3, 2]])","+    model_state._commit_eplb_maps(target)","+    assert model_state.committed_layers == [0]","+    torch.testing.assert_close(model_state.committed_maps[0], target)","+    torch.testing.assert_close(","+        model_state.logical_to_physical_map[0, :, 0], torch.tensor([1, 0, 3, 